  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/denticeps-clupeoides-2/",
      "html": "<p>Denticeps clupeoides is a small freshwater herring. It grows to a maximum length of 15 cm, but specimens over 8 cm in length are very rarely encountered.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/denticeps-clupeoides-2/",
      "html": "<p>Herring can usually only be kept in the aquarium with enormous effort; moreover, most species live in the sea. The species is somewhat sensitive to transport because of the high oxygen demand, but is imported from time to time.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/denticeps-clupeoides-2/",
      "html": "<p>It lives in larger shoals near the surface in rivers in western Africa; the specimens described here come from Nigeria.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/denticeps-clupeoides-2/",
      "html": "<p>The chemical water composition is of secondary importance for the care. These fish love strong currents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/denticeps-clupeoides-2/",
      "html": "<p>Feeding is easy: any commercially available ornamental fish food, including dry food, is accepted, however Denticeps do not like to eat from the bottom.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/denticeps-clupeoides-2/",
      "html": "<p>These restless swimmers are interesting aquarium fishes with much to be explored. They are peaceful animals that should only be kept together with other completely peaceful fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/denticeps-clupeoides-2/",
      "html": "<p>Breeding reports are not available yet.</p>"
    }
  ],
